{"id": "section-body-13509", "title": "Urticaria and Angioedema", "chapterId": "chapter-thirteen", "blocks": [{"id": "body-13509", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Urticaria and Angioedema", "runs": [{"text": "Urticaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Angioedema"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1368"}}, {"id": "body-13510", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Urticaria is the sudden development of transient wheals (superficial dermal swellings) and angioedema (deep dermal swellings) or both. It can be acute or chronic, spontaneous or inducible. It can be induced by viral infections, bacterial infections, food allergies, drug allergies, colds, heat, or tight clothing, among other factors.", "runs": [{"text": "Urticaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sudden"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "development"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "wheals"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(superficial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dermal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swellings)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "angioedema"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(deep"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dermal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swellings) or both. It can be acute or chronic, spontaneous or inducible. It can be induced by viral infections, bacterial infections, food allergies, drug allergies, colds, heat, or tight clothing, among other factors."}]}, {"id": "body-13512", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation:", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-13513", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Wheals that come and go rapidly within 24 hours", "runs": [{"text": "Wheals"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "come"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text"